{
  "name": "base_tree",
  "version": "2.0",
  "description": "A tree. The trunk is a cone -- wider at the root than at the crown -- rather than a cylinder with a taper modifier on it, because a taper's sign is easy to get backwards and a tree standing on a spike is what that looks like. The canopy is four spheres welded and remeshed into one crown and then displaced; left as separate spheres it reads as a snowman, which is what this recipe built before. Trunk and crown stay separate objects so they can take a bark material and a leaf material.",
